<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chenes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chenes is a region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a> state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, and the name of a Maya architectural style of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-classic-period">Late Classic period</a> that developed there. Chenes buildings are known for facades covered with stone mosaic masks, often framing doorways in the shape of a monster's open mouth. Hochob and Santa Rosa Xtampak are among its main sites, and the style also appears at Edzná.</p></div>
